#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Check before you create (exact-title search), create the bean when none exists, find out whose it is, and claim it — or leave it alone when a sibling holds it. Process_BeanOpen is the one place a claim is drawn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:105
#. Diagram label
msgid "claimed"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:71
#. Diagram label
msgid "Durable work identified"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Editing a bean is not a separate ceremony: check off todo items as they happen, append measurements with the command and date that produced them, and record what you now know that the next agent does not. A bean whose body is a title is a placeholder, not a plan."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "End the bean in a state that says why: done is completed and archived, not wanted is scrapped with its reasons and archived, blocked records what it waits on and goes back to `todo`. Process_BeanClose is the one place resolve and archive are drawn."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:104
#. Diagram label
msgid "not yours"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:73
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:60
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns every transition on a bean it holds. Whether the bean is its own at all is decided inside Process_BeanOpen, whose sibling lane takes someone else's bean; this lane only reads the answer at GW_Yours and stops when it is not."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress, so work it. `not yours`: someone else holds it and nothing was written; stop here rather than resolve, scrap or edit a bean you do not own."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:100
#. Diagram label
msgid "State recorded"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:49
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The whole life of a work-plan item, drawn the way every bean-touching process now runs it: OPEN the bean (check before you create, find out whose it is, claim it or leave it alone), do the work keeping the body current, then CLOSE it in a state that says why (complete and archive, scrap with reasons and archive, or record the blocker and hand back). You are in this process the moment durable work is identified — which is before the first tool call, not after the work is done. The two halves are called processes, Process_BeanOpen and Process_BeanClose, so the rules live in one place: a process that works on a bean calls the first where the bean becomes its own and the second before each end it reaches from there. The one irreversible thing is refused outright. Unwanted work is SCRAPPED with its reasons, never deleted, because a scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end while a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:84
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work, keeping the body current (this is 'edit')"
msgstr ""
